  "explains": "get_invoice in app/handlers/invoices.py changes (its return line). The spec api/openapi.json names the operation GET /invoices/{invoiceId} with operationId getInvoice, and the handler tree (app/handlers/*.py) has the function get_invoice, the snake_case form of that name, so the handler is found by name and nothing looser. The route is the server base path of the spec, /v1 (the url of its only server), then the path of the operation: GET /v1/invoices/{invoiceId}, cited at the method key, the path key and the server url line of the spec. On the web side the copy of the spec in the web repository gives the same URL and the method GET to the generated function getInvoice, which only fetchInvoice in src/modules/invoices/api.ts calls (its pages import fetchInvoice, not getInvoice); InvoiceDetailPage imports fetchInvoice and the invoices routes file mounts that page at /invoices/:invoiceId. voidInvoice, in the same page, is a DELETE: a different operation of the same path that the changed GET handler does not serve. InvoiceListPage and NewInvoicePage use other generated functions. The names get and list (generic words) and downloadStatement (defined four times) are dropped and recorded.",
  "complete_for": [
    "changed_symbol",
    "route",
    "http_edge",
    "screen"
  ],
